# Ops/support trust anchor — baked into the appliance image and appended to
# /root/.ssh/authorized_keys. This is the PUBLIC key of the Ctrlable ops/support identity,
# the one the portal's Wetty SSH gateway (ssh.ctrlable.com) and operators on the WireGuard VPN
# use to reach the bare-metal HOST over the tunnel for troubleshooting. Its private half stays
# with ops / the portal — never on the appliance. Scoped to human recovery and rotatable
# independently of the orchestrator automation key (that one is for orchestrator->host only).
#
# TODO(release): replace the placeholder below with the real ops public key before any
# production build. Rotate = ship a new image or OTA an authorized_keys update. For dev /
# boot-test images, build-rootfs.sh also honours an OPS_PUBKEY env var (appended as-is).
#
# ssh-ed25519 AAAA...REPLACE-WITH-OPS-PUBKEY... ctrlable-ops
